The rule as written for conformance.kernel.refusal-phrase says: "The first listed refusal phrase the reply contains, typographic apostrophes read as straight, or NONE." In the input, both "I can't" and "I cannot" are present. The first listed phrase is "I cannot", so the check's answer should be "I cannot". In the rewritten text, only "I cannot" is present, so the answer should still be "I cannot". Therefore the rule says the answer ought to be unchanged. However, the implementation returns the first occurring phrase, so it would move from "I can't" to "I cannot". This is a defect.